  "headword": "{睨|にら}みつける",
  "reading": "にらみつける",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to glare at, to stare down",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "ichidan",
    "stem": "{睨|にら}みつけ"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to glare at, to stare down, to fix with a piercing look",
      "explanation": "To look at someone or something with an intense, hostile, or intimidating gaze. Stronger and more aggressive than simply looking hard at something."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "13683_niramitsukeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{相手|あいて}を{睨|にら}みつける。",
      "english": "To glare at the opponent.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "13683_niramitsukeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{先生|せんせい}に{睨|にら}みつけられて、{黙|だま}ってしまった。",
      "english": "The teacher glared at me and I fell silent.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "13683_niramitsukeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{猫|ねこ}が{窓|まど}の{外|そと}の{鳥|とり}を{睨|にら}みつけて{動|うご}かなかった。",
      "english": "The cat fixed its gaze on the bird outside the window and didn't move.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\nAn intensified form of {睨|にら}む (to glare). The ～つける ending adds the nuance of directing the gaze firmly and fixedly at a target. Typically takes the particle を to mark the person or thing being glared at.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {相手|あいて}を{睨|にら}みつける: to glare at one's opponent\n- じっと{睨|にら}みつける: to glare fixedly\n- {鋭|するど}い{目|め}で{睨|にら}みつける: to glare with sharp eyes",
